 "pitfalls": [
  "Only the colour names the components use matter: a name the document defines replaces the theme's everywhere; a name it does not define keeps the default (dark) theme value, so check every component you call (track, outline, muted, success, warning, error, ...)",
  "Theme numbers (radii, spacing, text sizes) are substituted when the components expand and cannot be overridden per document; only colours re-theme",
  "The outlined Button fills its inside with `surface` (default @colors.background); here it sits on the page background so the default is right, but inside a Card pass surface: \"@colors.surface\"",
  "Colours stay named in the .rc (NAMED_VARIABLE), so a host can override them again at run time",
  "A row of buttons sized by their labels overflows a narrower host: the last one is squeezed, and the Button label is one line with an ellipsis, so give the row room (or fewer buttons) where every label must stay readable"
 ]
}
